          "final_text_tail": "added `import json`, `import json_repair`, and `model_validator` from pydantic.\n2. **`ToolCalls.validate_input`** \u2014 a `@model_validator(mode=\"before\")` classmethod (matching the existing pattern in `Code`, `Image`, `Audio`) that normalizes varied formats into the canonical structure while returning plain Python structures (not a `ToolCalls` instance):\n   - Dict with a `tool_calls` key \u2192 returned unchanged (existing behavior preserved).\n   - Single `{\"name\":..., \"args\":...}` object (no `tool_calls` key) \u2192 wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": [obj]}`.\n   - Bare list of such objects \u2192 wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": [...]}`.\n   - JSON string \u2192 parsed, then normalized by the rules above.\n   - Non-JSON string \u2192 returned unchanged.\n3. **`_parse_json_lenient`** helper \u2014 parses JSON with `json.loads` first, falling back to `json_repair.loads` for slightly malformed input; returns the original string when nothing parseable is found (guards against `json_repair` silently turning non-JSON into `''`).\n\n**Verification:**\n- All 8 behavior cases from the clarification pass (canonical dict, single object, bare list, JSON strings of each shape, non-JSON string, dict with `tool_calls` + extra keys).\n- Construction paths work: `ToolCalls(tool_calls=...)`, `ToolCalls.model_validate(single_obj)`, `ToolCalls.model_validate(bare_list)`.\n- All 88 existing adapter tests pass; `ruff format --check` passes. The one `ruff` `F811` warning (`Type` redefinition) is pre-existing on `HEAD`, not introduced by my change.",
